From: Simon McVittie <smcv@collabora.com>
Subject: Use O_PATH and O_CLOEXEC when opening parent directories

Backport of containers/bubblewrap#807, merged upstream in 0f8073d:
  2d81c15de37a21275c1a0912d0feab3c4842666d
  e45ef35bdfbe6536fc40bbb937295bb02cdf3bb5
https://github.com/containers/bubblewrap/pull/807

Opening a parent for path traversal must not require read permission. Keep
openat_in_root's RESOLVE_IN_ROOT and RESOLVE_NO_MAGICLINKS containment intact.

diff --git a/bubblewrap.c b/bubblewrap.c
--- a/bubblewrap.c
+++ b/bubblewrap.c
@@ -1044 +1044 @@ ensure_newroot_parents_at (const char *path,
-  cleanup_fd int parent_fd = openat_in_root ("/newroot", "/", O_DIRECTORY);
+  cleanup_fd int parent_fd = openat_in_root ("/newroot", "/", O_DIRECTORY | O_PATH | O_CLOEXEC);
@@ -1074 +1074 @@ ensure_newroot_parents_at (const char *path,
-      cleanup_fd int new_parent_fd = openat_in_root ("/newroot", fn, O_DIRECTORY);
+      cleanup_fd int new_parent_fd = openat_in_root ("/newroot", fn, O_DIRECTORY | O_PATH | O_CLOEXEC);
